<!--
  sce:std/shared/record_recall.scxml — a change a host gives back to a copy of a shared
  record list it builds again (docs/adr/0083, section 1.5; docs/adr/0085, section 7.2;
  docs/adr/0093, section 2.1): the copy's own, as it offered it (record_made) and the
  host journalled it, or another copy's, as the host's delivery layer holds it. A copy
  is built from what was made, never from the commands it was made from, so a rebuild
  makes no change again.

  The fields are record_made's: `by`, `wallTime` and `counter` (the change's author and
  stamp), `ops` (its operations, record_op, in the change's order) and `command` (the
  host's name for the command that ended it, 0 for a change of another copy); and
  `provisional`, whether the change is one of the copy's own that its layer had not
  carried yet when the host journalled it (docs/adr/0093, section 3.5), which the copy
  takes in provisionally, as it did at its verdict, so that a withdrawal after a
  restart behaves as one before it. The flag is read for a change of the copy's own
  node only.

  The host gives every change after the stable snapshot (record_list.restore,
  record_restore) in a causal order, its journal's and its layer's history's alike, and
  the copy takes each in whole by the one path every change is taken in by, judging no
  roster (each was admitted where it was made or carried), and sends and reports
  nothing. A recalled change of the copy's own raises its clock to the change's stamp,
  a write-over-only change included, and another's moves it as a peer's change does.

  The event is new with the journal, and its first revision carries `provisional`
  (docs/adr/0085, "Owner's answers"): a field of the first revision has no default, so
  a host writes it on every recall.
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml"
       xmlns:sce="http://sce.dev/ext"
       version="1.0"
       sce:kind="event-schema"
       name="record_recall"
       sce:event-name="record_list.recall">
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/shared/record_op.scxml" as="Op"/>
  <datamodel>
    <data id="by" sce:type="uint64" sce:direction="in"/>
    <data id="wallTime" sce:type="int64" sce:direction="in"/>
    <data id="counter" sce:type="uint32" sce:direction="in"/>
    <data id="ops" sce:type="list&lt;record:Op&gt;[1..shared_parts=64]" sce:direction="in"/>
    <data id="command" sce:type="uint64" sce:direction="in"/>
    <data id="provisional" sce:type="bool" sce:direction="in"/>
  </datamodel>
</scxml>
